From bc7d1cba6dee390beba0785e50935275d3f1d484 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: metaneutrons <436979+metaneutrons@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 15:37:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] module-raop-sink: encode all audio iovecs at ring-buffer wrap

The RTP producer supplies two frame-aligned audio segments when a packet
crosses the ring-buffer boundary. The RAOP callback encoded only the first
segment while the producer advanced by the full packet size, losing
samples from the second segment.

Encode all segments into one uncompressed ALAC frame without allocation
or a staging copy. Add a Meson regression that captures datagrams from the
actual sender callback and compares the contiguous packet with all 353
split positions, including empty boundary segments.

On master b0b792fa7, the unmodified callback fails 352 of 354 cases; the
fix passes all cases under ASan/UBSan with b_ndebug=true. The existing
RAOP RTSP client test also passes. Controlled PipeWire 1.6.7 live UDP
comparisons independently reproduce the fix on Linux aarch64 and x86_64.

Index: repo/src/modules/meson.build
